\0
The Imperium's hover technology proved to be a considerable tactical advantage in most ground engagements. The ability of Imperium armor to move over water allowed them to dictate the circumstances of conflicts, and made it difficult for even the most capable Freedom Guard commanders to marshal decisive victories. The Freedom Guard felt they must obtain this technology in order to challenge the Imperium's dominion. The Freedom Guard discovered an Imperium research base on the planet Malik, where advances to the hover drive were being developed, and assaulted the base in an attempt to steal the vital technology.
\1
The research facility is not heavily guarded as its location is believed to be unknown. Steal the Imperium hover technology, so that we can attempt to develop a hover driven weapon of our own. Then level the complex.
\n\n
\cOBJECTIVES\n
-->Use your Infiltrator to steal the plans for\n
\s\s\s\s the Hover Freighter\n
-->Destroy the Hover Research Facility\n\n

Tip: Morph your infiltrator into an enemy infantry unit so that you can enter his base without detection.  With the Infiltrator out of the enemy's line-of-sight, select the Infiltrator and press 'I' to get the morph cursor.  Click on the enemy infantry to morph into it.  Enter the enemy's HQ, Training Facility or Assembly Plant to steal plans for buildings and units.  Once you've obtained the plans, eject the Infiltrator from the building, and return him to your own HQ so that you can build the new technology.

\2
Your actions are praiseworthy.\n
\n
\cHISTORICAL OUTCOME:\n
While attempting to hunt down the infiltrator who had stolen their hover technology, the Imperium force on Malik was waylaid by a larger Freedom Guard regiment and destroyed. Unhindered the Freedom Guard went on to devastate the entire research facility. With the stolen information, Freedom Guard scientists were quickly able to develop a hover tank of their own.
\3
I fear you do not appreciate the importance of your goal.

